scatter_add on gfx1010 (Navi10, RDNA1) is already correct through the generic
atomic-add kernel. The dim=0 case with a broadcast index and matching trailing
dimensions (the PyG message-passing shape) is the common hot path, and
index_add_ computes the same result for it. On gfx1010 only, that one shape is
routed through index_add_; every other shape falls through to the stock kernel.
This is a performance path, not a correctness fix.

Gated at runtime on gcnArchName starting with "gfx1010", so it is inert on
gfx803 and on every other arch, and on CUDA builds.

NOT YET RE-VERIFIED ON REAL HARDWARE: applies to ROCm/pytorch release/2.14; not built or run on a gfx1010 card.

